  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Little Darling, Pal of Mine**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [2]\n- **Beaumont Rag**: back after 63 archived shows (442 days) [2]\n- **Blue Railroad Train**: back after 133 archived shows (917 days); rare: 3 archived performances [2]\n- **What Does the Deep Sea Say**: back after 63 archived shows (442 days); rare: 5 archived performances [2]\n- **Watson Blues**: back after 133 archived shows (917 days); rare: 5 archived performances [2]\n- **Smoke! Smoke! Smoke! (That Cigarette)**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [2]\n- **If I Needed You**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [2]\n- **Don't Think Twice, It's All Right**: back after 133 archived shows (917 days); rare: 5 archived performances [2]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **billystrings2025-09-05** (recommended): source not stated; 29 songs; 131 min [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Performed at The Woodward Theatre, part of the Bluegrass Music Hall of Fame & Museum, with Bryan Sutton on guitar and Royal Masat; Billy Strings played banjo [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **billystrings2025-09-05**: taped by Mr. Mountjoy; transferred by Mr. Mountjoy; source: Shure MV88 > iPhone 13 > Motiv Audio App > WAV [1]. Also: Transfer path: WAV file, tracked in CD Wave Editor, then converted to 24-bit/48kHz FLAC [1]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Poster by @BillybaseDotNet: [Billy Strings Woodward Theatre 2025 - Dual Night Poster Regular - BillyBase](https://billybase.net/merch/woodward-theatre-2025-dual-night-poster-regular/) [3]\n- Fan art by @BillybaseDotNet: [Billy Strings Woodward Theatre 2025 - N2 Poster Regular - BillyBase](https://billybase.net/merch/woodward-theatre-2025-n2-poster-regular/) [4]",
